Window-rule coverage under different sampling schemes on the SAME rule.
The conjecture ranges over Fin 8 -> R.  There is no canonical measure there,
so any 'fraction covered' is a property of the scheme, not of the problem.

  sampling scheme                  n  covered %
  integers [1,20]               4000     43.75%
  integers [1,40]               4000     42.27%
  integers [1,200]              4000     41.95%
  uniform reals [1,10]          4000     84.95%
  uniform reals [1,100]         4000     45.50%
  log-uniform [1,1000]          4000      1.80%
  AP +/-10%                     4000     61.62%
  AP +/-50%                     4000     50.10%
  clustered w/ outliers         4000     16.75%

spread across schemes is the answer: if the number moves, it is not a
fraction of the conjecture -- it is a pass rate on one enumeration.
